Third-party code in this repository
===================================

This project is distributed under the MIT license (see LICENSE). Two groups of
files come from elsewhere and keep their own terms. The split below was checked
against the upstream repositories on 2026-09-25, not inferred from file names.

1. Derived from phacility/xhprof (Apache License 2.0)
----------------------------------------------------

  src/Core/XhprofLib/**            report rendering, statistics, run storage
  src/html/js/xhprof_report.js     carries the upstream Facebook/Apache header
  src/html/css/xhprof.css          rewritten for this project's UI, upstream file was xhprof.css

phacility/xhprof is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://github.com/phacility/xhprof). Those files are used and modified under
that license. The modifications are the ten-framework adapters, the i18n layer,
the diagnosis section, and the fixes recorded in this repository's history —
each derived PHP file carries an Apache header stating this.

2. Redistributed third-party front-end libraries
------------------------------------------------

src/html/ also ships libraries authored elsewhere, which the report page loads
(or once loaded):

  jquery/jquery-3.0.0.min.js                    jQuery 3.0.0 (jQuery Foundation, MIT)
  js/bootstrap.min.js, css/bootstrap.css        Bootstrap 3.3.5 (MIT — header present)
  js/jquery.dataTables.min.js                   DataTables 1.10.15 (MIT) — byte-identical
                                                 to the 1.10.15 release
  js/dataTables.bootstrap.js, css/dataTables.bootstrap.css
                                                DataTables/Bootstrap integration; these two
                                                are the 1.x-era files, **not** 1.10.15
  images/sort_both.png, images/sort_desc.png    DataTables sort icons
                                                (referenced by css/dataTables.bootstrap.css)
  jquery/indicator.gif                          the loading spinner; kept because it is the
                                                only GIF used as a MIME fixture in the tests

Their own license terms apply (jQuery, Bootstrap and DataTables are MIT-licensed
upstream); where the upstream file shipped a license header it is kept verbatim.

Removed in this change: `jquery/jquery-1.2.6.js`, `jquery/jquery.autocomplete.{js,css}`,
`jquery/jquery.tooltip.{js,css}` (vendored by phacility/xhprof, last used by a tooltip
library that predates jQuery 3) and `js/bootstrap-table.js` + its Chinese locale file
(unreferenced). They are recoverable from this repository's history.
